{
  "manufacturer": "Vaisala",
  "manufacturer_slug": "vaisala",
  "model": "HPP272 hydrogen peroxide, humidity and temperature probe (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "hpp272",
  "short_model": "HPP272",
  "aliases": [
    "HPP272",
    "PEROXCAP HPP272"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (H2O2 / humidity probe)",
  "applies_to": "HPP272 vaporized hydrogen peroxide probe, Modbus RTU interface (user guide M211972EN-G).",
  "summary": "The HPP272 is a Vaisala PEROXCAP probe for vaporized hydrogen peroxide bio-decontamination that also measures humidity and temperature. It is a Modbus RTU slave on RS-485. This map covers H2O2, humidity and temperature readings, status codes, sensor vitality, compensation, purge, low-H2O2 threshold and analog-output settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The guide numbers registers in decimal starting at 1 and also prints the 0-based hex address used in the request; register number 1 is address 0x0000 on the wire."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "HPP272 User Guide",
    "doc_number": "M211972EN-G",
    "revision_date": "2023-04",
    "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M211972EN-G/en-US",
    "pages": "Appendix A Modbus reference, pp. 93-110 (Tables 11-22)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16.",
    "32-bit floats and 32-bit integers put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB). The guide states this and its worked read example confirms it.",
    "Unavailable data reads as quiet NaN (float) or 0x8000 (16-bit integer) rather than an exception.",
    "Left out: the restore-factory-settings register, because the guide prints its number (7937) and hex address (1E00) inconsistently and 7937 is also the signed-integer test register.",
    "Measurement status registers 533-542 use the same coding as 529-532 and are left out to keep the map short.",
    "Clipping and error-limit registers for the analog outputs (1801-1807, 2057-2063) and the service agreement block (2817-2846) are left out.",
    "Status code registers 514 and 516 are 32-bit values, so they follow the low-word-first rule for 32-bit integers."
  ],
